<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="FCO" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Foundational Concepts and Objectives</title>

  <subsection xml:id="subsec-p8">
    <title>Purpose</title>
    <p>
        The purpose of this lab is to explore how biodiversity within an ecosystem change over time in response to various environmental pressures. 
        By simulating a forest community and introducing real-world threats such as habitat loss, pollution, disease, overharvesting, invasive species, and climate change, students will gain a deeper understanding of the factors that influence species survival and ecosystem stability.
    </p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="subsec-LO8">
    <title>Learning Objectives</title>
  <p> You will: </p>
<ul>
    <li>
        <p>
            <term>LO 8.1:</term> Define biodiversity and explain its importance in maintaining ecosystem health.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            <term>LO 8.2:</term>Differentiate between extinction, extirpation, and endangerment and describe how population changes signal biodiversity loss.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            <term>LO 8.3:</term>Identify major threats to biodiversity, including habitat degradation, pollution, disease, overharvesting, invasive species, and climate change.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            <term>LO 8.4:</term>Identify major threats to biodiversity, including habitat degradation, pollution, disease, overharvesting, invasive species, and climate change.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            <term>LO 8.5:</term>Interpret graphical data to evaluate trends in species populations and relate these trends to ecological concepts.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            <term>LO 8.6:</term>Explain the ecological consequences of biodiversity loss for communities and ecosystems.
        </p>
    </li>
</ul>
</subsection>

